  m_text: 'In the early months of 1968, you are being presented with a complex, interwoven
    crisis: as a U.S. policymaker, you must balance military success, diplomatic
    credibility, domestic politics, and social stability, knowing that failure in
    one area can cascade into others. Every decision will have real consequences
    for soldiers, civilians, allies, the American public, and global perception of
    U.S. power. What comes next will be a direct result of your decisions. Choose
    wisely. '
